====================================================================================================
FLOOR over the whole bank: exact R' and minorant R'_min
====================================================================================================
  EXACT  R' floor over bank = 0.47337  at S=[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 84]
  => the coupling R' >= 0.4734 on this bank (the Node-3 quantity).

  INTERPRETATION:
   L(S) = R' * meas(R-safe) * meas(Q-lonely).
   - meas(Q-lonely) >= c_r (apex block) : CLOSED uniformly by the minorant (part 2).
   - R' >= c_R' (coupling)              : bounded below on the bank; the OPEN Node-3 floor.
   - meas(R-safe) > 0                   : the 14-free wide-part loneliness.
   The minorant CROSS sum shows the coupling is carried by the |N|=1 apex-14 cross-level
   (7 in R, m=1 in Q), with a super-polynomial tail in |N| -- a UNIFORM (band-free) tail.

DONE.
